---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LearnerPathControls from '../../components/LearnerPathControls.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/') ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
---

<BaseLayout title="Adult Path | Soroban Dojo" description="Follow a structured soroban self-study path for adults with practical first-week rhythm, confidence checks, and steady next steps.">
  <section class="path-studio-hero panel" style={`--path-mist:url('${base}graphics/worksheet-mist.svg')`}>
    <div class="path-studio-brand">
      <div class="path-studio-mark" aria-hidden="true"><img class="theme-decoration" src={`${base}graphics/sakura-mark.svg`} alt="" /></div>
      <div class="content-prose">
        <p class="eyebrow">Adult path · おとな</p>
        <h1>Structured self-study with practical rhythm</h1>
        <p>This path keeps explanations direct, practice disciplined, and progress easy to continue across short study sessions.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="path-studio-stats">
      <article class="subtle-panel path-studio-stat"><span>Best worksheet</span><strong>One-rod or mixed focus</strong></article>
      <article class="subtle-panel path-studio-stat"><span>Session length</span><strong>10–20 minutes</strong></article>
      <article class="subtle-panel path-studio-stat"><span>Best next tool</span><strong>Study plan</strong></article>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button" href={`${base}lessons/l0/parts-of-the-soroban`}>Start the first lesson</a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href={`${base}levels/l0`}>Open Foundations</a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href={`${base}study-plan`}>Open study plan</a>
    </div>
    <LearnerPathControls preferredPath="adults" heading="Use the structured self-study route for this learner" compact />
  </section>

  <section class="panel content-prose route-card compact-card">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Who this route is best for</p>
        <h2>Choose this path for steadier self-study blocks</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="muted">Use the children path instead if the learner needs shorter sessions, warmer reinforcement, and lighter first-week pacing.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .path-studio-hero{display:grid;gap:1rem;border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--hero-border) 55%, transparent);box-shadow:0 18px 48px color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 8%, transparent);background-image:var(--hero-overlay), var(--path-mist);background-size:cover;background-position:center bottom}
    .path-studio-brand{display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:flex-start}.path-studio-mark{width:4.5rem;height:4.5rem;border-radius:1.5rem;background:color-mix(in srgb, var(--panel-raised) 80%, transparent);display:grid;place-items:center;box-shadow:0 12px 32px color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 12%, transparent);flex:0 0 auto}.path-studio-mark img{width:3.25rem;height:3.25rem}.path-studio-stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.85rem}.path-studio-stat{display:grid;gap:.35rem}.path-studio-stat span{font-size:.75rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--accent)}@media (max-width:900px){.path-studio-stats{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
  </style>

  <section class="split-grid">
    <article class="panel content-prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">First week</p>
      <h2>A practical starter rhythm</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Day 1:</strong> Learn parts and place value without rushing into arithmetic.</li>
        <li><strong>Day 2:</strong> Read and set two-rod numbers until the layout feels predictable.</li>
        <li><strong>Day 3:</strong> Add and subtract on one rod in one focused practice session.</li>
        <li><strong>Day 4:</strong> Use one worksheet or daily drill pack to test recall under light pressure.</li>
        <li><strong>Day 5:</strong> Review weak points in practice mode instead of pushing to a new topic too early.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="muted">Consistency matters more than length. Ten honest minutes count.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="panel content-prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">First win</p>
      <h2>A clean confidence check</h2>
      <p>By the end of the first week, this path aims for one clean reading-and-calculation loop: understand place value, read a two-rod number, and complete one short one-rod problem without guessing.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button" href={`${base}lessons/l0/parts-of-the-soroban`}>Start the week</a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href={`${base}lessons/l0/reading-two-rod-numbers`}>Read the first win</a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href={`${base}exercises/l1/add-four-and-four`}>Solve the first win</a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href={`${base}paths/children`}>Compare the children path</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="panel content-prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Best next steps</p>
    <h2>After the basics feel stable</h2>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button" href={`${base}study-plan`}>Open study plan</a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href={`${base}daily-drills`}>Generate a daily drill pack</a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href={`${base}practice`}>Open structured practice</a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href={`${base}worksheets?preset=one-rod-focus`}>Use the one-rod worksheet</a>
      </div>
    </section>
</BaseLayout>
